// orient_exp_migrated_spelling.ri — CLI fixture pinning that the fix the
// #6080 `E_RotationVectorDimension` diagnostic RECOMMENDS actually works.
//
// The diagnostic tells the user to "spell every component as a dimensioned
// literal: `vec3(0rad, 0rad, 1.5708rad)` / `vec3(0deg, 0deg, 90deg)`". This
// fixture is those two spellings verbatim, so the advice is executable rather
// than merely plausible: `reify eval` must exit 0 and print two quaternions,
// not `undef`.
//
// It guards the amendment to the earlier advice, which named a lone component
// (`1.5708rad` / `90deg`). Followed literally on a rotation vector that gives
// `vec3(0, 0, 1.5708rad)` — a MIXED-dimension vec3 that collapses to `undef`
// before `orient_exp` runs, reproducing the exact silent failure #6080 set out
// to remove. See orient_exp_partial_migration.ri for that case.
//
// Unlike its sibling fixtures this one is CLEAN (no diagnostic, exit 0).

module orient_exp_migrated_spelling

structure def OrientExpMigratedSpelling {
    let q = orient_exp(vec3(0rad, 0rad, 1.5708rad))
    let p = orient_exp(vec3(0deg, 0deg, 90deg))
}
